  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Learn how A. oryzae tolerates inhibitors released by lignocellulose pretreatment, to engineer strains that grow on lignocellulosic side streams.",
    "experimental_design": "Pre-grown RIB40 mycelium was moved to Czapek-Dox fructose medium (28 °C) with or without an inhibitor at its IC50 and sampled 0, 1, 3, 5 and 24 h later; the atlas holds the control and furfural (2.3 mM) series.",
    "main_finding": "Most inhibitors caused ROS-linked stress with an early shutdown of cell-cycle, ribosome and ER protein-folding pathways, and strong induction of NAD(P)H-dependent oxidoreductases and ABC/MFS efflux transporters; aldehydes (especially HMF) caused the strongest response."
  },
